NAME
       fatlabel - show or change the label of a FAT (vfat) file system

SYNOPSIS
       fatlabel DEVICE [NEW-LABEL]

DESCRIPTION
       With only DEVICE, fatlabel prints the vfat file system's label. With
       NEW-LABEL it sets it. FAT labels are at most 11 characters; use
       capitals, because lowercase labels may not work on other systems
       (the tools warn about them). Unmount the file system first.

       mkfs.vfat -n LABEL sets a label when the file system is made.

EXAMPLES
           fatlabel /dev/vdb2 USBDATA
           blkid /dev/vdb2

SEE ALSO
       mkfs.fat(8), fsck.vfat(8), blkid(8), e2label(8)
